== 5. new note, non-blocking, measured rather than speculated ==

N1: `citationProse`'s doc comment is now behind its code. It still says "Inline code may use
any matching backtick-run length; an unmatched delimiter is prose, not a span" and says nothing
about the line bound that is the whole point of the fix. With `[^`\n]` in the body, a
multi-backtick span whose body CONTAINS a backtick is no longer matched as a unit:

  "`` `Behaviour 9` ``"     -> "  "               excluded (delimiters consumed as empty
                                                  spans, then the inner span is removed)
  "``Behaviour 9 `x` ``"    -> "Behaviour 9  "    LEAKS
  "``Behaviour 9``"         -> ""                 excluded
  "the literal `Behaviour 9` is fixture" -> "the literal  is fixture"  excluded

Corpus census of that shape: 20 multi-backtick spans, 18 with a backtick in the body, and
exactly 2 carrying a Behaviour citation — both `` `Behaviour 9` `` in W-084's own brief, both
in the excluded column above. ZERO instances of the leaking shape in 57 briefs, and
out-of-range is 0, so nothing is hidden. Worth one comment line, not a round: the comment
should say a span is line-bounded and that a multi-backtick body containing a backtick is not
recognised as one span.

